<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<dxl:DXLMessage xmlns:dxl="http://greenplum.com/dxl/2010/12/">
  <dxl:Comment><![CDATA[
    Objective: A multivariate ndistinct statistics object that covers only
    some of the grouping columns supplies the measured number of groups of
    the columns it covers. That joint count multiplies undamped; only the
    columns no object covers are damped against each other. Here stts covers
    a, b (9 groups) and c (5 distinct values) is uncovered, so the estimate
    is 9 x 5 = 45, the actual count. Damping the joint count like a single
    column gave 9 x 5 x 0.75^2 = 26.

    CREATE TABLE t (a INT, b INT, c INT);
    INSERT INTO t SELECT i % 3, i % 9, i % 5 FROM generate_series(1, 1000) s(i);
    CREATE STATISTICS stts (ndistinct) ON a, b FROM t;
    ANALYZE t;
    EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, TIMING OFF) SELECT COUNT(*) FROM t GROUP BY a, b, c;
                                                  QUERY PLAN
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Gather Motion 3:1  (slice1; segments: 3)  (cost=0.00..431.14 rows=45 width=8) (actual rows=45 loops=1)
       ->  HashAggregate  (cost=0.00..431.14 rows=15 width=8) (actual rows=30 loops=1)
             Group Key: a, b, c
             ->  Seq Scan on t  (cost=0.00..431.01 rows=334 width=12) (actual rows=667 loops=1)
     Optimizer: GPORCA
  ]]>
  </dxl:Comment>
